NAME
       printf - format and print data

SYNOPSIS
       printf format [arguments...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes ARGUMENTS under the control of FORMAT. The format is
       reused from the beginning until every argument is consumed.

       Conversions: %s %d %i %u %x %X %o %c and %%.
       Escapes: \n \t \r \a \b \f \v \e and \\.
       \NNN writes a byte from one to three octal digits, \xNN from one
       or two hex digits, so any byte can be written directly:

         printf '\xd0\xaf\n'        prints the letter Я
         printf 'red: \e[31mx\e[0m\n'

EXAMPLES
       printf '%s is %d years old\n' Cervus 1

SEE ALSO
       echo(1)
